MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Corazon feels like a natural next listen because Santana's guitar playing connects with the Clapton and Hendrix records I recently explored.",
    "The Beatles fit my interest in classic rock songwriting, while Norah Jones offers a quieter, piano-centered connection to You Should Be So Lucky."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "A broad 80s compilation and Patsy Cline's traditional country do not connect closely enough with the blues and guitar-led rock I want right now.",
    "Greatest Hits and Definitive Collection leave me unable to identify the artist or musical connection, so I would not choose them during a brief visit."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to assume that familiar older music is enough to interest me, when the playing and songwriting matter more than the era.",
    "Several collections suggest that wanting classic artists means wanting their greatest hits, although my recent listening has centered on individual albums."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The strongest connection for me is expressive guitar playing across blues and rock, which makes Corazon more compelling than loosely related familiar music.",
    "Something can fit my broader taste without being what I want today: the Beatles and quieter piano-led music appeal, but I would only try Corazon on this visit."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my classic rock interests but miss how strongly my current choice depends on blues-rooted guitar playing and a clear connection to recent albums."
}
